/' ORB-99 – [Manual Boot] Select Golden Payload

This scenario validates that, upon power-up or reset, the OrbSight V2 platform 
successfully boots from the golden payload stored in the QSPI 
after setting the slot selection parameter. The system must load both FreeRTOS (hart4) 
and U-Boot (hart1–3). FreeRTOS must emit a heartbeat, and Linux should boot into userspace.

Covered requirements:
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0001: Boot Sequence with Fallbacks
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0002: Boot report generation
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0003: Software image identification by boot SW
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0004: Boot report accessibility
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0008: Independent execution of Linux and FreeRTOS
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0009: Execution time of software image
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0011: The boot SW interface requirement
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0010: Payload integrity validation (MD5)
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0014: Payload composition (FreeRTOS + U-Boot)
- ORB-BSW-BOOT-0015: Boot Report on Linux
- ORB-BSW-HBM-0001: Heartbeat Feature
'/

@startuml ORB-99: [Manual Boot] Select Golden Payload
!include ../../params.puml
!include ../../conf.puml
!include ../../macros.puml

title
  |= Auto Boot Fallback Cases |= $c(ID) |= $c(ExpectedBootLog1)  |= $c(ExpectedBootLog2)     |= $c(Time) |
  | Fallback to eMMC0          | 10     | "MMC1 slot 10..."      | "MMC1 very magic passed"  | 10s       |
  | Fallback to eMMC1          | 20     | "MMC2 slot 20..."      | "MMC2 very magic passed"  | 10s       |
  | Fallback to SPI-FLASH      | 30     | "SPI-FLASH slot 30..." | "SPI very magic passed"   | 15s       |
  | Fallback to QSPI-FLASH     | 40     | "QSPI slot 40..."      | "QSPI very magic passed"  | 20s       |
end title

:Flash valid payloads (FreeRTOS + U-Boot + Linux with MD5) into all slots;
$simAction():Start monitoring CAN bus;

while ($c(Case) in //"Boot Source Cases"//)

  :Set boot slot selection parameter to $c(ID);
  $simCheck():* Read `boot_selection` parameter via CAN or Ethernet
  * Confirm that the value matches $c(ID)}
  $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0011")

  :Reboot the system;
  :Wait $c(Time) for system to boot;

  :Ping the system over Ethernet until response is received;
  $simCheck():* Measure boot time from power-on to first ping response
  * Ensure it is below $c(Time)}
  $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0009")

  fork
    :Download boot report via Ethernet;

    $simCheck():* Check that the file `boot_report.txt` exists in `/home/root/...`
    * Confirm that its timestamp is after the reboot
    * Confirm that it includes both HSS and Linux boot logs}
    $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0015, ORB-BSW-BOOT-0002")
    $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0004, ORB-BSW-BOOT-0008")

    $simCheck():* Confirm that the system booted from SlotID = $c(ID)
    * Check boot log for:
    - $c(ExpectedBootLog1)
    - $c(ExpectedBootLog2)
    * Confirms boot sequence and slot selection}
    $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0001, ORB-BSW-BOOT-0003")

    $simCheck():* Verify payload integrity check using MD5:
     - "MD5 read: ..."
     - "MD5 calc: ..."
     - MD5 passed"}
    $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0010")

    $simCheck():* Confirm both FreeRTOS and U-Boot images are loaded:
     - "boot_service(u54_1)::Processing boot image: \"u-boot.bin\""
     - "boot_service(u54_4)::Processing boot image: \"freertos.elf\""}
    $req("ORB-BSW-BOOT-0013")

  fork again
    :Observe FreeRTOS heartbeat on CAN;
    $simCheck():* Message ID 0x8001 received periodically (e.g., every 1s)}
    $req("ORB-BSW-HBM-0001")
  end fork

endwhile

$simAction():Stop monitoring CAN bus;
stop
@enduml